.TH SCRIPTING 7 "August 2026" "toha3ee 0.1.0" "toha3ee"
.SH NAME
scripting \- the toha3ee scripting language
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scripts are plain-text
.I .toha3ee
files executed by the console's script engine. They let you drive repeated
engagements: start modules, wait for conditions, branch on inventory state
and emit progress.
.PP
Validate a script without sending a single packet:
.RS
toha3ee build scripts/full-pipeline.toha3ee
.RE
Execute it for real (root required for most modules):
.RS
sudo toha3ee script scripts/full-pipeline.toha3ee
.RE
.SH SYNTAX
Each line is one statement. Module control:
.RS
on net.scan
.br
off service.synscan
.br
stop net.scan
.RE
One-shot modules:
.RS
exec -> report.generate
.RE
Configuration:
.RS
set arp.spoof.targets 10.0.0.5,10.0.0.6
.br
get arp.spoof.targets -> _targets
.RE
Progress and output:
.RS
echo -> "scanning hosts"
.RE
.SH CONDITIONS AND BRANCHING
.PP
.B Conditionals
.RS
if hosts.count >= 3
.br
\	on service.synscan
.br
else
.br
\	exec -> net.ping
.br
end
.RE
.PP
.B Module state conditions
.RS
if net.scan is running
.br
if net.scan is not running
.br
if "10.0.0.5" contains "10.0.0"
.RE
.PP
.B Compound conditions
.RS
and / or, e.g. "hosts.count >= 3 && dns.spoof is not running"
.RE
.SH WAITING
.PP
.B wait for
blocks until a module stops (or times out):
.RS
on net.scan
.br
wait for net.scan max 60
.br
echo -> "scan finished"
.RE
.SH VARIABLES
.PP
Variables start with an underscore; assign with
.IR -> ,
.IR = ,
or
.IR >> ,
and interpolate with
.BR "$(name)" :
.RS
_target -> 10.0.0.1
.br
echo -> "scanning $(_target)"
.RE
.SH STRINGS
.PP
Double-quoted strings interpolate
.BR "$(...)" ;
single-quoted strings are literal (no escapes, no interpolation). Unquoted
values such as IPs, CIDRs and command flags like
.B -sS
are taken verbatim.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR toha3ee (1),
.BR security (7)
.PP
The full language reference lives in the repository's
.I docs/scripting.md
.
